From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <bmc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hostnamed: allow networkd transient hostname without polkit

The board uses networkd and hostnamed without polkit. DHCP UseHostname=true
therefore fails authorization for the systemd-network user. Resolve that
user's UID and use hostnamed's existing good_user authorization only for
SetHostname in builds without polkit. Lookup failure leaves authorization
unchanged. Static hostname and machine-info setters keep their checks.

Keep hostnamed running as root so Web static hostname writes still work;
do not give networkd CAP_SYS_ADMIN or install a polkit daemon.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific authorization policy]
---
--- a/src/hostname/hostnamed.c
+++ b/src/hostname/hostnamed.c
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@
 #include "strv.h"
 #include "time-util.h"
 #include "utf8.h"
+#include "user-util.h"
 #include "varlink-io.systemd.Hostname.h"
 #include "varlink-io.systemd.service.h"
 #include "varlink-util.h"
@@ -1331,6 +1332,7 @@
 static int method_set_hostname(sd_bus_message *m, void *userdata, sd_bus_error *error) {
         Context *c = ASSERT_PTR(userdata);
         const char *name;
+        uid_t network_uid = UID_INVALID;
         int interactive, r;
 
         assert(m);
@@ -1351,11 +1353,20 @@
 
         name = substituted;
 
+#if !ENABLE_POLKIT
+        /* DHCP may update only the transient hostname. Keep the privileged
+         * hostnamed service and all other setters' authorization unchanged. */
+        const char *network_user = "systemd-network";
+        r = get_user_creds(&network_user, &network_uid, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0);
+        if (r < 0)
+                network_uid = UID_INVALID;
+#endif
+
         r = bus_verify_polkit_async_full(
                         m,
                         "org.freedesktop.hostname1.set-hostname",
                         /* details= */ NULL,
-                        /* good_user= */ UID_INVALID,
+                        /* good_user= */ network_uid,
                         interactive ? POLKIT_ALLOW_INTERACTIVE : 0,
                         &c->polkit_registry,
                         error);
